# Force LF line endings on export/checkout regardless of the local
# machine's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, `git archive` (used by
# the new-project-from-template skill to seed a new project with no
# shared history) converts LF -> CRLF on a Windows machine with
# core.autocrlf=true, which breaks the bash scripts once they run inside
# a Linux container -- e.g. a CRLF-corrupted `set -euo pipefail` line
# fails with "set: pipefail: invalid option name" since bash reads the
# trailing \r as part of the option name. text=auto still lets git detect
# genuine binary files (images, etc.) and leaves those untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
